# Material 3 UI

- Use MUI Material 3 components (`@mui/material`, icons from `@mui/icons-material`).
- Theme with MD3 tokens: color roles (primary, secondary, tertiary, surface, outline), typography scale, shape, elevation/shadows.
- Prefer theme `sx` / `styled` over one-off CSS files for component styling.
- Wrap the app with MUI `ThemeProvider` + CssBaseline (and Next.js App Router cache provider when required).
- Prefer built-in MUI primitives: Button, TextField, Select, Dialog, Drawer, AppBar, Data Grid (if tables are needed), Snackbar/Alert.
- Do not mix another component library. Custom components should compose MUI primitives.
- Keep density and spacing consistent with the theme (`theme.spacing`).
- Support light/dark via theme color schemes when the product enables them.

```tsx
// ✅ Theme-driven styling
<Button variant="filled" color="primary" sx={{ borderRadius: 2 }}>
  Save
</Button>

// ❌ Ad-hoc styling that bypasses the theme
<button className="rounded bg-blue-500 px-4 py-2 text-white">Save</button>
```
